 </eslint-code-block>
 
+The rule also reports removable alternatives inside nested groups and elements of non-negated character classes. For example, the `a` in `/a+|[abc]/` can be removed, and `/a+|[a-f]/` can be simplified to `/a+|[b-f]/`. Range interiors are kept: `/c+|[a-f]/` is not reported with the default options.
+
